  "applies": true,
  "fixmes": [],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`src/evidence.rs#fn[validate_input]` takes a parameter named `errors` and collects repository-validation errors. It is therefore a site of `requirements.ci.errors`.\n\nThe requirement obliges a site to run every later check that does not depend on a failed check's result, and not to report one failure twice. The function meets both obligations.\n\nViolation matches:\n- `return None` when the input is not a JSON object is harmless. The error is pushed first, and no later check can run without an object.\n- `definition?` is harmless. `check_keys`, `string_field` and `text_field` have all run and reported before it. Only the resolution step depends on `definition`, and the code comment says resolving it does not depend on a well-formed `text`.\n- `requirements?` is harmless for the same reason. `check_keys`, `string_field`, the `matches` validation and `text_field` have all run first. Resolution depends only on `requirements`. A malformed `text` or `matches` becomes `None`, and `validate_resolved_input` skips only the comparison that depends on that field.\n- The two `return validate_resolved_input(...)` expressions are tail hand-offs, so nothing is skipped after them. The final call to `validate_outline_input` is likewise the last step.\n\nThe helpers show no double reporting:\n- `text_field` checks every element rather than stopping at the first bad one.\n- The `matches` closure reports non-string entries and duplicates as separate failures.\n- `check_keys`, `string_field` and `array_field` each report distinct conditions.\n- Each message starts with `label` and names the failed check and value, in the style of a `requirements.ci.validation_error`.\n\nI found no gap.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/evidence.rs",
      "item": "fn[validate_input]",
      "hash": "ba071d68ab65d0a7893dd005cc03d35444c368ee68181a7835b3ed2806d2ebf0"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
